<title>USA: SanDisk seeks pact with Samsung.</title>
<headline>SanDisk seeks pact with Samsung.</headline>
<dateline>SUNNYVALE, Calif. 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>SanDisk Corp said it is negotiating a definitive settlement agreement with Samsung Electronics Co Ltd and Samsung Semiconductor Inc to cover all disputes under investigation by the U.S. International Trade Commission.</p>
<p>The ITC has agreed at the parties' request to delay completion of its investigation until June 2, SanDisk said. A final agreement is subject to approval by both parties and the ITC.</p>
<p>In February, an ITC judge ruled that Samsung Electronics and Samsung Semiconductor had infringed two SanDisk U.S. patents involving flash memory.</p>
<p>SanDisk is the world's largest supplier of flash data storage products.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
